    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 **52 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain blocklist rule for owner creation using the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (not Spring MVC). `POST /api/owners` now rejects with 400 when the owner's email domain is `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, or `guerrillamail.com`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **New function** `RequireNonDisposableOwnerEmail.java` \u2014 reads the validated body (`@Val OwnerFieldsDto`), skips when email is absent/blank, extracts the domain (case-insensitively), and throws `OwnerEmailDisposableException` when it's on the blocklist.\n\n2. **New checked exception** `OwnerEmailDisposableException.java` \u2014 carries the offending email, mirroring the existing `OwnerEmailInvalidException`.\n\n3. **New handler** `OwnerEmailDisposableExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 400 with `{\"errors\": [\"email\"]}`, matching the existing email-error handler.\n\n4. **New escalation YAML** mapping the exception to the handler.\n\n5. **Wired the step** into `owners.POST.yml` immediately after `normalizeEmail` (so syntax is already validated and the email is lower-cased) and before `cityCapacity`, under the same `transaction` governance as the surrounding steps.\n\nThe pre-existing acceptance test `Cp38Tests.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (which was already present, referencing the blocklist) now passes, and all other tests remain green.",
